      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of possible outcomes when rolling four 6-sided dice.\n2. Calculate the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.\n3. Subtract the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number from the total number of possible outcomes.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of possible outcomes.**\n\nEach die has 6 faces, and since we are rolling 4 dice, the total number of possible outcomes is:\n\\[ 6^4 = 1296. \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number.**\n\nThere are 6 possible outcomes where all four dice show the same number (one for each face of the die: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6). So, there are 6 outcomes where all four dice show the same number.\n\n**Step 3: Subtract the number of outcomes where all four dice show the same number from the total number of possible outcomes.**\n\nThe number of outcomes where not all four dice show the same number is:\n\\[ 1296 - 6 = 1290. \\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the probability.**\n\nThe probability that not all four dice show the same number is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n\\[ \\frac{1290}{1296} = \\frac{215}{216}. \\]\n\nSo, the probability that when we roll four fair 6-sided dice, they won't all show the same number is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{215}{216}}. \\]",
